From b065754f3ff4e301c08c823c8ec940c93b1b064c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seto Kaiba <seto@ddl.local>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:49:41 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] r35.12 TEST branch: coin toss and dice roll get their own
 procedural sound effects (Kevy 30 Oct)

- dist/coin-cutscene.mjs: coinSound rewritten. Coin: flick + flip whoosh + spinning flutter, metallic shimmer,
  landing clink with two bounces and settling chatter, Heads/Tails result tail, then the call sting. Dice: rattle
  (one pitch per die), throw whoosh, tumble/hit/clatter/bounce, one settle thunk per die, pip chime per die.
  Hits sit on the animation keyframes. Fixed-seed variation from the toss (no Math.random). Nothing scheduled when
  sound is off, master 0, SFX 0 or audio not running. Still routed through the scene's own gain node (RELAY-068),
  so Skip cuts it at once. +5 dB (COIN_SFX_LEVEL 1.8) over the r35.10 cues.
- tests/r35.12-coin-dice-sfx.test.mjs (new), tools/r35.12-render-coin-dice-sfx.mjs (WAV previews),
  tools/r35.12-sfx-paired-duel.mjs (seed 71002 sound on/off paired duel). SOUND_CREDITS.md section.
- Untouched: AI, duel.mjs, random.mjs, worker.mjs, coin-tap.mjs, presentation.mjs, sound-engine.mjs, app.mjs,
  frozen gate files, RC1, labels (index.html / sw.js still r35.11). SELF-VERIFIED; for ChatGPT review.
