 ## r28 rendered sound effects (22 Oct 2026)
 Kevy asked for a robust, loud chain sound and more dynamic, epic moves and activations. `dist/audio/sfx/` now holds 28 rendered effects (MP3, about 1.3 MB): chain links 1, 2, 3 and 4+ (each heavier, longer and louder than the last), chain lock, a resolving link, Spell / Trap / monster / Field Spell activations, Equip, Normal / Special / Fusion / Synchro / Xyz / Link summons, a boss hit, card whooshes (to hand, to Graveyard, to Deck / field), banish, destroy, material, negate, attack, impact and cost. They are original: built by `tools/r28-render-sfx.py` from oscillators, filtered noise, envelopes, a synthetic reverb and soft saturation. The chain-link and resolve sounds also layer slices of the CC0 "Heavy chain" recording (BigSoundBank 0359, see `dist/audio/CREDITS.md`). No Konami or Master Duel audio. The synth cues stay as the fallback when the files are not loaded.
+
+## r35.12 coin toss and dice roll sounds (30 Oct 2026, TEST branch, not published)
+Kevy asked for the coin toss and dice roll cutscenes to have their own sound effects. They are original procedural Web Audio synthesis in `dist/coin-cutscene.mjs` (`coinSound`), built only on the existing `tone()` and `noise()` helpers of `dist/sound-engine.mjs` (oscillators, the engine's generated noise, envelopes and filters). Coin: a thumb flick, a rising and falling flip whoosh with a spinning flutter, a metallic shimmer, a landing clink with two bounces and a settling chatter, then a short Heads (bright, rising) or Tails (darker, falling) tail and the right / wrong call sting. Dice: a rattle with one pitch per die, a throw whoosh, a tumble with a table hit, rolling clatter and a bounce, then one settle thunk per die. No samples, recordings or downloads of any kind; no new licence dependencies. `tools/r35.12-render-coin-dice-sfx.mjs` renders previews for review only.
